From: EglantinePS5
Subject: up: write the pipelines a session used, in first-use order, as key hashes (EDEN_UP_FIRST_START_LIST_WRITE), off by default

What: with EDEN_UP_FIRST_START_LIST_WRITE=1 (and EDEN_UP_CANONICAL_KEYS=1) the first use
of every graphics pipeline (CurrentGraphicsPipelineSlowPath, after a pipeline exists; M when it
has a task/mesh stage, else G) and of every compute pipeline (a new one when it is made, a known
one at its first dispatch; C) is noted on the GPU thread as kind + the key's CityHash64. The list
goes to <title>/first_start.list every 30 s while it grows and at shutdown, on the serialization
thread (written beside and renamed over). The previous session's list is kept as
first_start.prev.list, so a short run does not wipe a useful one. At most 65,536 rows.

Header: "EDEN_FIRST_START_2 cache= driver= canonical= static_vertex= title= lowering=": what the
hashes depend on, so a reader can refuse a list of another build or key policy (review S1-B);
lowering= comes from the same constant as the shader set's identity. Not in it: the game version
(the video core has only the title id here). Rows: "G|M|C <16 hex>", and
"T <seconds> <rows before>" at each write, so a list made on a warm start can be cut by hand at
the door's time. No area marks: S1b's NotifyFirstStartAreaLoad had no caller (both reviews) and is
not ported. Contents: only fixed tags, decimal numbers and 64-bit key hashes; no code, no state
bytes, no answers, no addresses.

Off: one switch read in the constructor, one bool test per first use of a pipeline and per compute dispatch of a known one; nothing
allocated, written or logged. It changes nothing that is built or drawn. Nothing reads the list
in this build (the preparation from it, S1c, is left out: see our notes).

Credits: the list idea and the first draft (S1b): our own draft, reviewed twice;
first-start build rule: hckrman101 (NotRexed/Hookshot #2865, #2869).
